From 8b7bfe10ef3af74f9be3443ea08fcb4e060e964d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 03:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add join codes: a self-hostable rendezvous and relay
 service

bri-rendezvous gives each host a short code (K7Q-4MZ), tells a player
where the host is, has the host send a packet from its game port to the
player so both routers open (hole punching over QUIC), and relays the
still end-to-end encrypted game traffic when routers do not allow that.
It keeps nothing but its certificate, limits codes per IP, lookups per
minute and relay bandwidth, and prints the address players configure.

bri-net: JoinCodes is the provider boundary (ours is Rendezvous); hosts
hold a code from the game port's own endpoint; Client::connect_code races
every direct route against the relay (tried after 1.5 s) from one socket.
natsim simulates home routers (RFC 4787 mapping and filtering) behind
quinn's AsyncUdpSocket, so the loopback tests prove direct joins through
two port-restricted routers, relay joins through symmetric ones, and a
plain failure without a relay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
